We are given the expression (\sqrt{5}+\mathrm{i}) \cdot(\sqrt{5}-2 \mathrm{i}). We can expand this expression as follows:
\begin{align*} (\sqrt{5}+\mathrm{i}) \cdot(\sqrt{5}-2 \mathrm{i}) &= \sqrt{5} \cdot \sqrt{5} + \sqrt{5} \cdot (-2 \mathrm{i}) + \mathrm{i} \cdot \sqrt{5} + \mathrm{i} \cdot (-2 \mathrm{i}) \\ &= 5 - 2 \sqrt{5} \mathrm{i} + \sqrt{5} \mathrm{i} - 2 \mathrm{i}^2 \end{align*}
Since \mathrm{i}^2 = -1, we have
\begin{align*} 5 - 2 \sqrt{5} \mathrm{i} + \sqrt{5} \mathrm{i} - 2(-1) &= 5 - 2 \sqrt{5} \mathrm{i} + \sqrt{5} \mathrm{i} + 2 \\ &= 5 + 2 + (-2 \sqrt{5} + \sqrt{5}) \mathrm{i} \\ &= 7 + (-\sqrt{5}) \mathrm{i} \end{align*}
Thus, the expression simplifies to 7 - \sqrt{5} \mathrm{i}.

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{7-\sqrt{5}i}$

